        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): models advertise tools when /api/show fails",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users discovering local Ollama models would still see tool support advertised when `/api/show` failed (HTTP error or network throw), so a broken or uninspectable model looked tool-capable in catalog/setup paths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`buildOllamaModelDefinition` treats missing `capabilities` as optimistic `supportsTools: true`. Failed `/api/show` previously returned `{}`, which left capabilities undefined. This change marks failed inspection with `showInspectionFailed`, keeping three states:\n\n1. `capabilities` omitted (uninspected / successful show without field) → optimistic tools + name heuristics\n2. `capabilities: string[]` (including `[]`) → authoritative show result\n3. `showInspectionFailed` → tools conservative, reasoning name heuristics preserved\n\nThe failure marker is propagated through provider discovery, interactive setup config building, and the dynamic `/models add` resolve path (there is no `src/auto-reply/reply/models-add.ts` on current main; that sibling lives in `extensions/ollama/index.ts`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nLocal Ollama models whose `/api/show` fails no longer advertise tools across discovery, setup, and dynamic model resolve, while reasoning-named models still keep the established name heuristic during transient inspection failures. A successful show that reports an empty capabilities list remains authoritatively non-tool and non-reasoning.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Proof | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | three-state unit matrix + HTTP 404/throw paths | pass |\n| L2 | `buildOllamaProvider`, setup config build, dynamic resolve | pass |\n| L3 | Real `127.0.0.1` HTTP (`/api/tags` 200, `/api/show` 500) + undici `fetch` | pass |\n\n| Rank-up P1 fail-closed dynamic resolve | `resolveRequestedDynamicOllamaModel` returns `undefined` on `showInspectionFailed` (typo/404/throw stay rejected); tag/setup keep tools-off marker | tip `9d8f849ad9be` |\n| Gate | `pnpm exec oxfmt --check` + `oxlint` + `vitest run` on `index`/`setup`/`provider-models` tests → **126 passed** | local |\n\nScrapable L3 line:\n\n```text\n[ollama show-fail live proof] base=http://127.0.0.1:56531 model=deepseek-r1:14b showHits=1 supportsTools=false reasoning=true\n```\n\nLocal gates:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.test.ts extensions/ollama/index.ts extensions/ollama/index.test.ts\npnpm exec oxlint <same files>\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.test.ts extensions/ollama/index.test.ts\n→ 125 passed\n```\n\nHead: `9d8f849ad9bea52f0ff7f433fa4d50afc638d4da`\n",
